# Untitled UI-Inspired Design System

This project uses [Untitled UI](https://www.untitledui.com/react/) as **design inspiration**—similar aesthetic (clean, modern, neutral) but not a pixel-perfect copy. Implementation is **CSS-only** with a 3-layer design token system. No Tailwind.

---

# Design Inspiration

Untitled UI informs our visual language:

- Neutral gray palette with blue accent
- Consistent spacing scale (4px base)
- Subtle shadows and borders
- Clean typography (system font stack)

We aim for a similar feel without using Untitled UI components or Tailwind.

---

# Token Architecture

All styling flows through a **3-layer token system**. No component should reference raw colors or spacing directly.

**Layer 1 — Primitives** (`extension/src/styles/tokens/primitives.css`)

Raw design values. No UI meaning.

- Colors: `--gray-100`, `--gray-900`, `--blue-500`, etc.
- Spacing: `--space-1` through `--space-8`
- Radius: `--radius-1` through `--radius-4`
- Typography: `--font-sans`, `--font-mono`
- Shadows: `--shadow-sm`, `--shadow-md`, `--shadow-lg`

**Layer 2 — Semantic** (`extension/src/styles/tokens/semantic.css`)

UI meaning mapped from primitives.

- `--color-text-primary`, `--color-text-secondary`, `--color-text-muted`
- `--color-surface`, `--color-surface-alt`, `--color-panel`
- `--color-border`, `--color-border-strong`
- `--color-accent`, `--color-accent-hover`, `--color-accent-subtle`
- `--color-overlay`, `--color-danger`

**Layer 3 — Component tokens**

Defined in each component root. Map to semantic or spacing tokens.

Example:

```css
.snippet-card {
  --card-bg: var(--color-panel);
  --card-border: var(--color-border);
  --card-radius: var(--radius-2);
  --card-padding: var(--space-3);
  --card-shadow-hover: var(--shadow-md);

  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: var(--card-radius);
  padding: var(--card-padding);
}
```

---

# Load Order

In each entry (popup, library):

1. `styles/tokens/index.css`
2. `styles/base.css`
3. Component CSS (popup/styles.css, library/styles.css)

---

# Content Script Overlay

The capture confirmation modal ([`extension/src/content/capture-confirmation-modal.ts`](extension/src/content/capture-confirmation-modal.ts)) runs in page context with Shadow DOM. It cannot import extension CSS.

It must inject a `<style>` block that defines the same primitive and semantic variables (via `tokens-css.ts` or raw import) so the modal matches the extension UI visually.

---

# Icons

Use Lucide or Feather icons (per ui-design.mdc). Do not use `@untitledui/icons`.

---

# Hard Rules

Do NOT:

- hardcode colors, spacing, or radius in components
- reference primitive tokens inside component style rules (use semantic or component tokens)
- reference semantic tokens directly in deeply nested elements (create component tokens)

Always:

- create component tokens for each component
- map component tokens to semantic or spacing tokens
- follow the 3-layer architecture for all new UI

---

# No Runtime Themes

This project does not support runtime theme switching. All tokens are fixed in CSS. To change the look, edit `primitives.css` and/or `semantic.css`.
